{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('update7.json'))\ne=d['experiment']\ne['previous_id']='6b30dd76d4b64190be2808a0e7abb041-experiment'\ne['revision_reason']=(\\\"The predecessor execution failed at its snapshot step (receipt 4ed46b198c8d41618cc855df0a63d469, exit 1, 'snapshot on A failed: nothing new to snapshot'; \\\"\n \\\"the initial leader was C rather than A). This revision makes the case deterministic and self-terminating: leadership is transferred to A through the library's own transfer before the snapshot, \\\"\n \\\"a command is committed and awaited in A's FSM before the snapshot request, and every node is shut down on all exit paths. Four local construction runs of the revised harness reproduce the \\\"\n \\\"predicate; the predecessor receipt is retained as an explained harness failure, not as a comparison result.\\\")\ne['semantic_changes']=[\n \\\"Leadership is moved to A with LeadershipTransferToServer before the snapshot, because the election winner is arbitrary and removing the leader (ShutdownOnRemove defaults to true) would shut it down; the predecessor removed whichever node C was even when C led.\\\",\n \\\"The pre-snapshot command is committed through A and the harness waits until A's FSM has applied a command entry, because runFSM refuses a snapshot request while its own last applied index is zero and a plain MockFSM never observes configuration or no-op entries.\\\",\n \\\"Every node is shut down on all exit paths so no raft goroutine logs through the test logger after the test returns, which panicked the predecessor's later iterations.\\\"\n]\nd['rationale']=(\\\"The predecessor execution failed on a harness race, so this batch resubmits the fixed experiment for the open gap with a deterministic leadership setup and explicit shutdow